:null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02354548172811942,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.3,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010442070730970905,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.43727002,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Slide Insurance Holdings, Inc. provides property and casualty insurance services in the United States. The company writes coastal specialty personal lines insurance, including homeowners, condominium unit owners, commercial residential, and other products, as well as offers reinsurance and insurance agency services. Slide Insurance Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bruce Thomas Lucas J.D. | Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 53 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 652 people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $1.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Slide Insurance Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.0B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The business throws off $795M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 69 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.80\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 44% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 22% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 80% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 70% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Slide Insurance (NASDAQ:SLDE) Stock: Insider Beth Witte Bruce Sells 25,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/slide-insurance-nasdaqslde-stock-insider-beth-witte-bruce-sells-25000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388989.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Slide Insurance Holdings (SLDE) On Earnings And Dividend News Looks Modestly Undervalued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-slde/slide-insurance-holdings/news/slide-insurance-holdings-slde-on-earnings-and-dividend-news","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793996979.709,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"What Does Slide Insurance Holdings (SLDE) Entry Into Texas And Rhode Island Mean?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-slde/slide-insurance-holdings/news/what-does-slide-insurance-holdings-slde-entry-into-texas-and","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906613.015,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Slide Insurance (NASDAQ:SLDE) Cut to Hold at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/slide-insurance-nasdaqslde-cut-to-hold-at-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793688176.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Slide Insurance Holdings (SLDE) Q3 Earnings Spotlight Underwriting Strength And Coastal Risk","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-slde/slide-insurance-holdings/news/slide-insurance-holdings-slde-q3-earnings-spotlight-underwri","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp"